Lex["490"] = "Antiocheia {an-tee-okh'-i-ah}|AV - Antioch 18; 18|from Antiochus (a Syrian king)||noun proper location|Antioch = 'driven against\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> Capital of Syria, situated on the river Orontes, founded by Seleucus Nicanor in 300 B.C. and named in honour of his father, Antiochus. Many Greek-Jews lived there and it was here that the followers of Christ were first called Christians.INDENT0--<b>2)</b> A city in Pisidia on the borders Phrygia, founded by Seleucus Nicanor. Under the Romans it became a \"colonia\" and was also called Caesarea<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Ἀντιόχεια Anti&#xF3;cheia, an-tee-okh&#39;-i-ah; from &#x1F08;&#x3BD;&#x3C4;&#x1F77;&#x3BF;&#x3C7;&#x3C5;&#x3C2; Ant&#xED;ochys (a Syrian king); Antiochia, a place in Syria:&#8212;Antioch.";
