Lex["683"] = "apotheomai {ap-o-theh'-om-ahee} or apothomai {ap-o'-thom-ahee}|AV - cast away 2, thrust away 1, put from 1, thrust from 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;put away 1; 6|from 575 and the middle voice of otheo or otho (to shove)|TDNT - 1:448,*|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to thrust away, push away, repelINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to thrust away from one's self, to drive away from one's selfINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> repudiate, reject, refuse<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>ἀπωθέομαι ap&#x14D;th&#xE9;omai, ap-o-theh&#39;-om-ahee; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=575&page=1\">G575</a> and the middle voice of &#x1F60;&#x3B8;&#x1F73;&#x3C9; &#x14D;th&#xE9;&#x14D; or &#x1F64;&#x3B8;&#x3C9; &#x1E53;th&#x14D; (to shove); to push off, figuratively, to reject:&#8212;cast away, put away (from), thrust away (from).";
