Lex["714"] = "arkeo {ar-keh'-o}|AV - be content 3, be sufficient 2, be enough 1, suffice 1, content 1; 8|apparently a primary word [but probably akin to 142 through the idea of raising a barrier]|TDNT - 1:464,78|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to be possessed of unfailing strengthINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to be strong, to suffice, to be enoughINDENT7--<b>1)</b> to defend, ward offINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to be satisfied, to be contented<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρκέω ark&#xE9;&#x14D;, ar-keh&#39;-o; apparently a primary verb (but probably akin to Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=142&page=1\">G142</a> through the idea of raising a barrier); properly, to ward off, i.e. (by implication) to avail (figuratively, be satisfactory):&#8212;be content, be enough, suffice, be sufficient.";
