Lex["743"] = "archaggelos {ar-khang'-el-os}|AV - archangel 2; 2|from 757 and 32|TDNT - 1:87,12|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> archangel, or chief of the angels<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />The Jews, after the exile, distinguished several orders of angels; some reckoned four angels (according to the four sides of God's throne) of the highest rank; but the majority reckoned seven (after the pattern of the seven Amshaspands, the highest spirits of the religion of Zoroaster)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχάγγελος arch&#xE1;ngelos, ar-khang&#39;-el-os; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=757&page=1\">G757</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=32&page=1\">G32</a>; a chief angel:&#8212;archangel.";
