Lex["745"] = "Archelaos {ar-khel'-ah-os}|AV - Archelaus 1; 1|from 757 and 2994||noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Archelaus = \"prince of the people\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> A son of Herod the Great by Malthace, the Samaritan woman. He and his brother Antipas were brought up with a certain private man in Rome. After the death of his father, he ruled as ethnarch over Judaea, Samaria and Idumaea, (with the exception of the cities of Gaza, Gadara and Hipo). The Jews and the Samaritans having accused him at Rome of tyranny, he was banished by the emperor Augustus to Vienna of the Allobroges and died there.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Ἀρχέλαος Arch&#xE9;laos, ar-khel&#39;-ah-os; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=757&page=1\">G757</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2994&page=1\">G2994</a>; people-ruling; Archelaus, a Jewish king:&#8212;Archelaus.";
Lex["746"] = "arche {ar-khay'}|AV - beginning 40, principality 8, corner 2, first 2, misc 6; 58|from 756|TDNT - 1:479,81|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> beginning, originINDENT0--<b>2)</b> the person or thing that commences, the first person or thing in a series, the leaderINDENT0--<b>3)</b> that by which anything begins to be, the origin, the active causeINDENT0--<b>4)</b> the extremity of a thingINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of the corners of a sailINDENT0--<b>5)</b> the first place, principality, rule, magistracyINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of angels and demons<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχή arch&#x1E17;, ar-khay&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=756&page=1\">G756</a>; (properly abstract) a commencement, or (concretely) chief (in various applications of order, time, place, or rank):&#8212;beginning, corner, (at the, the) first (estate), magistrate, power, principality, principle, rule.";
Lex["747"] = "archegos {ar-khay-gos'}|AV - prince 2, captain 1, author 1; 4|from 746 and 71|TDNT - 1:487,81|adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the chief leader, princeINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of ChristINDENT0--<b>2)</b> one that takes the lead in any thing and thus affords an example, a predecessor in a matter, pioneerINDENT0--<b>3)</b> the author<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχηγός arch&#x113;g&#xF3;s, ar-khay-gos&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=746&page=1\">G746</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=71&page=1\">G71</a>; a chief leader:&#8212;author, captain, prince.";
Lex["748"] = "archieratikos {ar-khee-er-at-ee-kos'}|AV - of the high priest 1; 1|from 746 and a derivative of 2413||adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> high priestly, pontifical<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχιερατικός archieratik&#xF3;s, ar-khee-er-at-ee-kos&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=746&page=1\">G746</a> and a derivative of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2413&page=1\">G2413</a>; high-priestly:&#8212;of the high-priest.";
Lex["749"] = "archiereus {ar-khee-er-yuce'}|AV - chief priest 64, high priest 58, chief of the priest 1; 123|from 746 and 2409|TDNT - 3:265,349|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> chief priest, high priest<BR><BR> He above all others was honoured with the title of priest, the chief of priests. It was lawful for him to perform the common duties of the priesthood; but his chief duty was, once a year on the day of atonement, to enter into the Holy of Holies (from which the other priests were excluded) and offer sacrifices for his own sins and the sins of the people, and to preside over the Sanhedrin, or Supreme Council, when convened for judicial deliberations. According to Mosaic law, no one could aspire to the high priesthood unless he were of the tribe of Aaron and descended from a high priestly family; and he on whom the office was conferred held it till death. But from the time of Antiochus Epiphanes, when the kings of Seleucideae and afterwards the Herodian princes and the Romans arrogated to themselves the power of appointing the high priests, the office neither remained vested in the pontifical family nor was conferred on any for life; but it became venal, and could be transferred from one to another according to the will of civic or military rulers. Hence it came to pass, that during the one hundred and seven years intervening between Herod the Great and the destruction of the holy city, twenty eight persons held the pontifical dignity. <BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>2)</b> the high priests, these comprise in addition to one holding the high priestly office, both those who had previously discharged it and although disposed, continued to have great power in the State, as well as the members of the families from which high priest were created, provided that they had much influence in public affairs. <BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>3)</b> Used of Christ because by undergoing a bloody death he offered himself as an expiatory sacrifice to God, and has entered into the heavenly sanctuary where he continually intercedes on our behalf.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχιερεύς archiere&#xFA;s, ar-khee-er-yuce&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=746&page=1\">G746</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2409&page=1\">G2409</a>; the high-priest (literally, of the Jews, typically, Christ); by extension a chief priest:&#8212;chief (high) priest, chief of the priests.";
Lex["750"] = "archipoimen {ar-khee-poy'-mane}|AV - chief shepherd 1; 1|from 746 and 4166|TDNT - 6:485,901|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> chief shepherdINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of Christ the head of the church<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχιποίμην archipo&#xED;m&#x113;n, ar-khee-poy&#39;-mane; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=746&page=1\">G746</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4166&page=1\">G4166</a>; a head shepherd:&#8212;chief shepherd.";
Lex["751"] = "Archippos {ar'-khip-pos}|AV - Archippus 2; 2|from 746 and 2462||noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Archippus = \"master of the horse\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a certain Christian teacher in Colosse<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Ἄρχιππος &#xC1;rchippos, ar&#39;-khip-pos; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=746&page=1\">G746</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2462&page=1\">G2462</a>; horse-ruler; Archippus, a Christian:&#8212;Archippus.";
Lex["752"] = "archisunagogos {ar-khee-soon-ag'-o-gos}|AV - ruler of the synagogue 7, chief ruler of the synagogue 2; 9|from 746 and 4864|TDNT - 6:844,1107|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> ruler of the synagogue. It was his duty to select the readers or teachers in the synagogue, to examine the discourses of the public speakers, and to see that all things were done with decency and in accordance with ancestral usage.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχισυνάγωγος archisyn&#xE1;g&#x14D;gos, ar-khee-soon-ag&#39;-o-gos; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=746&page=1\">G746</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4864&page=1\">G4864</a>; director of the synagogue services:&#8212;(chief) ruler of the synagogue.";
Lex["753"] = "architekton {ar-khee-tek'-tone}|AV - masterbuilder 1; 1|from 746 and 5045||noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a master builder, an architect, the superintendent in the erection of buildings<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχιτέκτων archit&#xE9;kt&#x14D;n, ar-khee-tek&#39;-tone; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=746&page=1\">G746</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5045&page=1\">G5045</a>; a chief constructor, i.e. \"architect\":&#8212;masterbuilder.";
Lex["754"] = "architelones {ar-khee-tel-o'-nace}|AV - chief among the publicans 1; 1|from 746 and 5057||noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a chief of tax collectors, chief publican<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχιτελώνης architel&#x1E53;n&#x113;s, ar-khee-tel-o&#39;-nace; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=746&page=1\">G746</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5057&page=1\">G5057</a>; a principle tax-gatherer:&#8212;chief among the publicans.";
Lex["755"] = "architriklinos {ar-khee-tree'-klee-nos}|AV - governor of the feast 2, ruler of the feast 1; 3|from 746 and a compound of 5140 and 2827 (a dinner-bed, because composed of three couches)||noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the superintendent of the dining room, a table master.<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />It differs from toast-master, who was one of the guests selected by lot to prescribe to the rest the mode of drinking. The table master was to place in order the tables and the couches, arrange the courses, taste the food and wine beforehand, and so forth.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἀρχιτρίκλινος architr&#xED;klinos, ar-khee-tree&#39;-klee-nos; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=746&page=1\">G746</a> and a compound of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5140&page=1\">G5140</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2827&page=1\">G2827</a> (a dinner-bed, because composed of three couches); director of the entertainment:&#8212;governor (ruler) of the feast.";
