Lex["1066"] = "Gedeon {ghed-eh-own'}|AV - Gedeon 1; 1|of Hebrew origin 01439||noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Gideon = \"the cutter down\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a of the judge of Israel who delivered them from the Midianites<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Γεδεών Gede&#x1E53;n, ghed-eh-own&#39;; of Hebrew origin (Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=H1439\">H1439</a>); Gedeon (i.e. Gid(e)on), an Israelite:&#8212;Gedeon (in the King James Version).";
Lex["1067"] = "geenna {gheh'-en-nah}|AV - hell 9, hell fire + 3588 + 4442 3; 12|of Hebrew origin 01516 and 02011|TDNT - 1:657,113|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> Hell is the place of the future punishment call \"Gehenna\" or \"Gehenna of fire\". This was originally the valley of Hinnom, south of Jerusalem, where the filth and dead animals of the city were cast out and burned; a fit symbol of the wicked and their future destruction.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> γέεννα g&#xE9;enna, gheh&#39;-en-nah; of Hebrew origin (Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=H1516\">H1516</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=H2011\">H2011</a>); valley of (the son of) Hinnom; ge-henna (or Ge-Hinnom), a valley of Jerusalem, used (figuratively) as a name for the place (or state) of everlasting punishment:&#8212;hell.";
