Lex["1125"] = "grapho {graf'-o}|AV - write 206, writing 1, describe 1, vr write 1; 209|a root word|TDNT - 1:742,128|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to write, with reference to the form of the lettersINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to delineate (or form) letters on a tablet, parchment, paper, or other materialINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to write, with reference to the contents of the writingINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to express in written charactersINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to commit to writing (things not to be forgotten), write down, recordINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> used of those things which stand written in the sacred books (of the OT)INDENT3-- <b>d)</b> to write to one, i.e. by writing (in a written epistle) to give information, directionsINDENT0--<b>3)</b> to fill with writingINDENT0--<b>4)</b> to draw up in writing, compose<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>γράφω gr&#xE1;ph&#x14D;, graf&#39;-o; a primary verb; to \"grave\", especially to write; figuratively, to describe:&#8212;describe, write(-ing, -ten).";
