Lex["1248"] = "diakonia {dee-ak-on-ee'-ah}|AV - ministry 16, ministration 6, ministering 3, misc 9; 34|from 1249|TDNT - 2:87,152|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> service, ministering, esp. of those who execute the commands of othersINDENT0--<b>2)</b> of those who by the command of God proclaim and promote religion among menINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of the office of MosesINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> of the office of the apostles and its administrationINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> of the office of prophets, evangelists, elders etc.INDENT0--<b>3)</b> the ministration of those who render to others the offices of Christian affection esp. those who help meet need by either collecting or distributing of charitiesINDENT0--<b>4)</b> the office of the deacon in the churchINDENT0--<b>5)</b> the service of those who prepare and present food<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> διακονία diakon&#xED;a, dee-ak-on-ee&#39;-ah; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1249&page=1\">G1249</a>; attendance (as a servant, etc.); figuratively (eleemosynary) aid, (official) service (especially of the Christian teacher, or technically of the diaconate):&#8212;(ad-)minister(-ing, -tration, -try), office, relief, service(-ing).";
