Lex["2176"] = "euonumos {yoo-o'-noo-mos}|AV - left 5, on the left hand 4, left foot 1; 10|from 2095 and 3686||adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> of good name and of good omenINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> in the latter sense used in taking auguries; but those omens were euphemistically called \"euonumos\" which in fact were regarded as unlucky, i.e. which came from the left, sinister omens, (for which a good name was desired)INDENT0--<b>2)</b> left, on the left hand<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> εὐώνυμος eu&#x1E53;nymos, yoo-o&#39;-noo-mos; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2095&page=1\">G2095</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3686&page=1\">G3686</a>; properly, well-named (good-omened), i.e. the left (which was the lucky side among the pagan Greeks); neuter as adverbial, at the left hand:&#8212;(on the) left.";
