Lex["2203"] = "Zeus {dzyooce}|AV - Jupiter 2; 2|of uncertain affinity||noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Jupiter or Zeus = \"a father of helps\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the national god of the Greeks and corresponds to the Roman Jupiter<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Ζεύς Ze&#xFA;s, dzyooce; of uncertain affinity; in the oblique cases there is used instead of it a (probably cognate) name &#x394;&#x1F77;&#x3C2; D&#xED;s deece, which is otherwise obsolete; Zeus or Dis (among the Latins, Jupiter or Jove), the supreme deity of the Greeks:&#8212;Jupiter.";
Lex["2204"] = "zeo {dzeh'-o}|AV - be fervent 1, fervent 1; 2|a primary verb|TDNT - 2:875,296|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to boil with heat, be hotINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> used of waterINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> metaph.INDENT7--<b>1)</b> used of boiling anger, love, zeal, for what is good or bad etc.INDENT7--<b>2)</b> fervent in spirit, said of zeal for what is good<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζέω z&#xE9;&#x14D;, dzeh&#39;-o; a primary verb; to be hot (boil, of liquids; or glow, of solids), i.e. (figuratively) be fervid (earnest):&#8212;be fervent.";
Lex["2205"] = "zelos {dzay'-los}|AV - zeal 6, envying 5, indignation 2, envy 1, fervent mind 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;jealousy 1, emulation 1; 17|from 2204|TDNT - 2:877,297|noun masculine/neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> excitement of mind, ardour, fervour of spiritINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> zeal, ardour in embracing, pursuing, defending anythingINDENT7--<b>1)</b> zeal in behalf of, for a person or thingINDENT7--<b>2)</b> the fierceness of indignation, punitive zealINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> an envious and contentious rivalry, jealousy<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζῆλος z&#x113;los, dzay&#39;-los; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2204&page=1\">G2204</a>; properly, heat, i.e. (figuratively) \"zeal\" (in a favorable sense, ardor; in an unfavorable one, jealousy, as of a husband (figuratively, of God), or an enemy, malice):&#8212;emulation, envy(-ing), fervent mind, indignation, jealousy, zeal.";
Lex["2206"] = "zeloo {dzay-lo'-o}|AV - zealously affect 2, more with envy 2, envy 1, be zealous 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;affect 1, desire 1, covet 1, covet earnestly 1, misc 2; 12|from 2205|TDNT - 2:882,297|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to burn with zealINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to be heated or to boil with envy, hatred, angerINDENT7--<b>1)</b> in a good sense, to be zealous in the pursuit of goodINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to desire earnestly, pursueINDENT7--<b>1)</b> to desire one earnestly, to strive after, busy one's self about himINDENT7--<b>2)</b> to exert one's self for one (that he may not be torn from me)INDENT7--<b>3)</b> to be the object of the zeal of others, to be zealously sought afterINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> to envy<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>ζηλόω z&#x113;l&#xF3;&#x14D;, dzay-lo&#39;-o; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2205&page=1\">G2205</a>; to have warmth of feeling for or against:&#8212;affect, covet (earnestly), (have) desire, (move with) envy, be jealous over, (be) zealous(-ly affect).";
Lex["2207"] = "zelotes {dzay-lo-tace'}|AV - zealous 5; 5|from 2206|TDNT - 2:882,297|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> one burning with zeal, a zealotINDENT0--<b>2)</b> used of God as jealous of any rival and sternly vindicating<BR> his controlINDENT0--<b>3)</b> most eagerly desirous of, zealous for, a thingINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to acquire a thing, (zealous of)INDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to defend and uphold a thing, vehemently contending for a thing<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζηλωτής z&#x113;l&#x14D;t&#x1E17;s, dzay-lo-tace&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2206&page=1\">G2206</a>; a \"zealot\":&#8212;zealous.";
Lex["2208"] = "Zelotes {dzay-lo-tace'}|AV - Zelotes 2; 2|the same as 2207|TDNT - 2:882,297|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> one burning with zeal, a zealotINDENT0--<b>2)</b> used of God as jealous of any rival and sternly vindicating his controlINDENT0--<b>3)</b> most eagerly desirous of, zealous for, a thingINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to acquire a thing, (zealous of)INDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to defend and uphold a thing, vehemently contending for a thing<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />From the time of the Maccabees there existed among the Jews a class of men, called Zealots, who vigorously adhered to the Mosaic law and endeavored &ndash; even by a resort to violence, after the example of Phinehas, to prevent religion from being violated by others. In the latter days of the Jewish commonwealth they used their holy zeal as a pretext for the basest crimes.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Ζηλωτής Z&#x113;l&#x14D;t&#x1E17;s, dzay-lo-tace&#39;; the same as Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2207&page=1\">G2207</a>; a Zealot, i.e. (specially) partisan for Jewish political independence:&#8212;Zelotes.";
Lex["2209"] = "zemia {dzay-mee'-ah}|AV - loss 3, damage 1; 4|probably akin to the base of 1150 (through the idea of violence)|TDNT - 2:888,299|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> damage, loss<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζημία z&#x113;m&#xED;a, dzay-mee&#39;-ah; probably akin to the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1150&page=1\">G1150</a> (through the idea of violence); detriment:&#8212;damage, loss.";
Lex["2210"] = "zemioo {dzay-mee-o'-o}|AV - lose 2, suffer loss 2, be cast away 1, receive damage 1; 6|from 2209|TDNT - 2:888,299|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to affect with damage, do damage toINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to sustain damage, to receive injury, suffer loss<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζημιόω z&#x113;mi&#xF3;&#x14D;, dzay-mee-o&#39;-o; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2209&page=1\">G2209</a>; to injure, i.e. (reflexively or passively) to experience detriment:&#8212;be cast away, receive damage, lose, suffer loss.";
Lex["2211"] = "Zenas {dzay-nas'}|AV - Zenas 1; 1|probably contracted from a poetic form of 2203 and 1435||noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Zenas = \"Jupiter\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a teacher of the Jewish law and afterwards a Christian<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Ζηνᾶς Z&#x113;n&#xE2;s, dzay-nas&#39;; probably contracted from a poetic form of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2203&page=1\">G2203</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1435&page=1\">G1435</a>; Jove-given; Zenas, a Christian:&#8212;Zenas.";
Lex["2212"] = "zeteo {dzay-teh'-o}|AV - seek 100, seek for 5, go about 4, desire 3, misc 7; 119|of uncertain affinity|TDNT - 2:892,300|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to seek in order to findINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to seek a thingINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to seek [in order to find out] by thinking, meditating, reasoning, to enquire intoINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> to seek after, seek for, aim at, strive afterINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to seek i.e. require, demandINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to crave, demand something from someone<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζητέω z&#x113;t&#xE9;&#x14D;, dzay-teh&#39;-o; of uncertain affinity; to seek (literally or figuratively); specially, (by Hebraism) to worship (God), or (in a bad sense) to plot (against life):&#8212;be (go) about, desire, endeavour, enquire (for), require, (X will) seek (after, for, means). Compare Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4441&page=1\">G4441</a>.";
Lex["2213"] = "zetema {dzay'-tay-mah}|AV - question 5; 5|from 2212||noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a question, debateINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> about the law<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζήτημα z&#x1E17;t&#x113;ma, dzay&#39;-tay-mah; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2212&page=1\">G2212</a>; a search (properly concretely), i.e. (in words) a debate:&#8212;question.";
Lex["2214"] = "zetesis {dzay'-tay-sis}|AV - question 6; 6|from 2212|TDNT - 2:893,300|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a seekingINDENT0--<b>2)</b> enquiryINDENT0--<b>3)</b> a questioning, debateINDENT0--<b>4)</b> a subject of questioning or debate, matter of controversy<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>ζήτησις z&#x1E17;t&#x113;sis, dzay&#39;-tay-sis; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2212&page=1\">G2212</a>; a searching (properly, the act), i.e. a dispute or its theme:&#8212;question.";
Lex["2215"] = "zizanion {dziz-an'-ee-on}|AV - tares 8; 8|of uncertain origin||noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a kind of darnel, resembling wheat except the grains are black<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζιζάνιον ziz&#xE1;nion, dziz-an&#39;-ee-on; of uncertain origin; darnel or false grain:&#8212;tares.";
Lex["2216"] = "Zorobabel {dzor-ob-ab'-el}|AV - Zorobabel 3; 3|of Hebrew origin 02216||noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Zerubbabel = \"born at Babel, i.e. Babylon\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the head of the tribe of Judah at the time of the return from Babylonish captivity in the first year of Cyrus<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Ζοροβάβελ Zorob&#xE1;bel, dzor-ob-ab&#39;-el; of Hebrew origin (Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=H2216\">H2216</a>); Zorobabel (i.e. Zerubbabel), an Israelite:&#8212;Zorobabel.";
Lex["2217"] = "zophos {dzof'-os}|AV - darkness 2, mist 1, blackness 1; 4|akin to the base of 3509||noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> darkness, blacknessINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> used of the darkness of the nether world<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζόφος z&#xF3;phos, dzof&#39;-os; akin to the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3509&page=1\">G3509</a>; gloom (as shrouding like a cloud):&#8212;blackness, darkness, mist.";
Lex["2218"] = "zugos {dzoo-gos'}|AV - yoke 5, pair of balances 1; 6|from the root of zeugnumi (to join, especially by a \"yoke\")|TDNT - 2:896,301|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a yokeINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> a yoke that is put on draught cattleINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> metaph., used of any burden or bondageINDENT7--<b>1)</b> as that of slaveryINDENT7--<b>2)</b> of troublesome laws imposed on one, esp. of the Mosaic law, hence the name is so transferred to the commands of Christ as to contrast them with the commands of the Pharisees which were a veritable 'yoke'; yet even Christ's commands must be submitted to, though easier to be keptINDENT0--<b>2)</b> a balance, pair of scales<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζυγός zyg&#xF3;s, dzoo-gos&#39;; from the root of &#x3B6;&#x3B5;&#x1F7B;&#x3B3;&#x3BD;&#x3C5;&#x3BC;&#x3B9; ze&#xFA;gnymi (to join, especially by a \"yoke\"); a coupling, i.e. (figuratively) servitude (a law or obligation); also (literally) the beam of the balance (as connecting the scales):&#8212;pair of balances, yoke.";
Lex["2219"] = "zume {dzoo'-may}|AV - leaven 13; 13|probably from 2204|TDNT - 2:902,302|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> leavenINDENT0--<b>2)</b> metaph. of inveterate mental and moral corruption, viewed in its tendency to infect others<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />Leaven is applied to that which, though small in quantity, yet by its influence thoroughly pervades a thing; either in a good sense as in the parable Mat. 13:33; or in a bad sense, of a pernicious influence, \"a little leaven leaveneth the whole lump\"<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζύμη z&#xFD;m&#x113;, dzoo&#39;-may; probably from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2204&page=1\">G2204</a>; ferment (as if boiling up):&#8212;leaven.";
Lex["2220"] = "zumoo {dzoo-mo'-o}|AV - leaven 4; 4|from 2219|TDNT - 2:902,302|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to leavenINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to mix leaven with dough so as to make it ferment<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζυμόω zym&#xF3;&#x14D;, dzoo-mo&#39;-o; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2219&page=1\">G2219</a>; to cause to ferment:&#8212;leaven.";
Lex["2221"] = "zogreo {dzogue-reh'-o}|AV - catch 1, take captive 1; 2|from the same as 2226 and 64||verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to take aliveINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to take, catch, capture<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζωγρέω z&#x14D;gr&#xE9;&#x14D;, dzogue-reh&#39;-o; from the same as Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2226&page=1\">G2226</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=64&page=1\">G64</a>; to take alive (make a prisoner of war), i.e. (figuratively) to capture or ensnare:&#8212;take captive, catch.";
Lex["2222"] = "zoe {dzo-ay'}|AV - life 133, lifetime 1; 134|from 2198|TDNT - 2:832,290|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> lifeINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> the state of one who is possessed of vitality or is animateINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> every living soulINDENT0--<b>2)</b> lifeINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of the absolute fulness of life, both essential and ethical, which belongs to God, and through him both to the hypostatic \"logos\" and to Christ in whom the \"logos\" put on human natureINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> life real and genuine, a life active and vigorous, devoted to God, blessed, in the portion even in this world of those who put their trust in Christ, but after the resurrection to be consummated by new accessions (among them a more perfect body), and to last for ever.<BR> <!--For Synonyms see entry 5821<br />--><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζωή z&#x14D;&#x1E17;, dzo-ay&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2198&page=1\">G2198</a>; life (literally or figuratively):&#8212;life(-time). Compare Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5590&page=1\">G5590</a>.";
Lex["2223"] = "zone {dzo'-nay}|AV - girdle 6, purse 2; 8|probably akin to the base of 2218|TDNT - 5:302,702|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a girdle, belt, serving not only to gird on flowing garments but also, since it was hollow, to carry money in<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζώνη z&#x1E53;n&#x113;, dzo&#39;-nay; probably akin to the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2218&page=1\">G2218</a>; a belt; by implication, a pocket:&#8212;girdle, purse.";
Lex["2224"] = "zonnumi {dzone'-noo-mi} or zonnuo {dzone-noo'-o}|AV - gird 2; 2|from 2223|TDNT - 5:302,702|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to girdINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to gird one's self<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ζώννυμι z&#x1E53;nnymi, dzone&#39;-noo-mi; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2223&page=1\">G2223</a>; to bind about (especially with a belt):&#8212;gird.";
Lex["2225"] = "zoogoneo {dzo-og-on-eh'-o}|AV - preserve 1, live 1; 2|from the same as 2226 and a derivative of 1096|TDNT - 2:873,290|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to bring forth aliveINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to give lifeINDENT0--<b>3)</b> to preserve alive<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>ζωογονέω z&#x14D;ogon&#xE9;&#x14D;, dzo-og-on-eh&#39;-o; from the same as Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2226&page=1\">G2226</a> and a derivative of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1096&page=1\">G1096</a>; to engender alive, i.e. (by analogy) to rescue (passively, be saved) from death:&#8212;live, preserve.";
Lex["2226"] = "zoon {dzo'-on}|AV - beast 23; 23|of a derivative of 2198|TDNT - 2:873,290|noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a living beingINDENT0--<b>2)</b> an animal, brute, beast<BR> <!--For Synonyms see entry 5846<br />--><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>ζῶον z&#x14D;on, dzo&#39;-on; neuter of a derivative of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2198&page=1\">G2198</a>; a live thing, i.e. an animal:&#8212;beast.";
Lex["2227"] = "zoopoieo {dzo-op-oy-eh'-o}|AV - quicken 9, give life 2, make alive 1; 12|from the same as 2226 and 4160|TDNT - 2:874,290|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to produce alive, begat or bear living youngINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to cause to live, make alive, give lifeINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> by spiritual power to arouse and invigorateINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to restore to lifeINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> to give increase of life: thus of physical lifeINDENT3-- <b>d)</b> of the spirit, quickening as respects the spirit, endued with new and greater powers of lifeINDENT0--<b>3)</b> metaph., of seeds quickened into life, i.e. germinating, springing up, growing<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>ζωοποιέω z&#x14D;opoi&#xE9;&#x14D;, dzo-op-oy-eh&#39;-o; from the same as Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2226&page=1\">G2226</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4160&page=1\">G4160</a>; to (re-)vitalize (literally or figuratively):&#8212;make alive, give life, quicken.";
Lex["2228"] = "e {ay}|AV - or 260, than 38, either 8, or else 5, nor 5,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;not tr 21, misc 20; 357|a primary particle of distinction between two connected terms||particle|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> either, or, than<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἤ &#x1E17;, ay; a primary particle of distinction between two connected terms; disjunctive, or; comparative, than:&#8212;and, but (either), (n-)either, except it be, (n-)or (else), rather, save, than, that, what, yea. Often used in connection with other particles. Compare especially Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2235&page=1\">G2235</a>, Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2260&page=1\">G2260</a>, Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2273&page=1\">G2273</a>.";
Lex["2229"] = "e {ay}|AV - surely + 3375 1; 1|an adverb of confirmation, perhaps intensive of 2228||adverb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> assuredly, most certainly, full surely<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἦ &#x113;, ay; an adverb of confirmation; perhaps intensive of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2228&page=1\">G2228</a>; used only (in the New Testament) before Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3303&page=1\">G3303</a>; assuredly:&#8212;surely.";
Lex["2230"] = "hegemoneuo {hayg-em-on-yoo'-o}|AV - be governor 2; 2|from 2232||verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to be leader, to lead the wayINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to rule, commandINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of a province, to be governor of a provinceINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> said of a proconsul, of a procurator<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἡγεμονεύω h&#x113;gemone&#xFA;&#x14D;, hayg-em-on-yoo&#39;-o; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2232&page=1\">G2232</a>; to act as ruler:&#8212;be governor.";
Lex["2231"] = "hegemonia {hayg-em-on-ee'-ah}|AV - reign 1; 1|from 2232||noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> chief command, rule, sovereigntyINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of the reign of a Roman emperor<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἡγεμονία h&#x113;gemon&#xED;a, hayg-em-on-ee&#39;-ah; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2232&page=1\">G2232</a>; government, i.e. (in time) official term:&#8212;reign.";
Lex["2232"] = "hegemon {hayg-em-ohn'}|AV - governor 19, ruler 2, prince 1; 22|from 2233||noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a leader of any kind, a guide, ruler, prefect, president, chief, general, commander, sovereignINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> a \"legatus Caesaris\", an officer administering a province in the name and with the authority of the Roman emperorINDENT7--<b>1)</b> the governor of a provinceINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> a procurator, an officer who was attached to a proconsul or a proprietor and had charge of the imperial revenuesINDENT7--<b>1)</b> in causes relating to these revenues he administered justice. In the smaller provinces also, which were so to speak appendages of the greater, he discharged the functions of governor of the province; and such was the relation of the procurator of Judaea to the governor of Syria.INDENT3-- <b>c)</b> first, leading, chiefINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of a principal town as the capital of the region<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἡγεμών h&#x113;gem&#x1E53;n, hayg-em-ohn&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2233&page=1\">G2233</a>; a leader, i.e. chief person (or figuratively, place) of a province:&#8212;governor, prince, ruler.";
Lex["2233"] = "hegeomai {hayg-eh'-om-ahee}|AV - count 10, think 4, esteem 3, have rule over 3, be governor 2,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;misc 6; 28|middle voice of a (presumed) strengthened form of 71|TDNT - 2:907,303|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to leadINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to go beforeINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to be a leaderINDENT7--<b>1)</b> to rule, commandINDENT7--<b>2)</b> to have authority overINDENT7--<b>3)</b> a prince, of regal power, governor, viceroy, chief, leading as respects influence, controlling in counsel, overseers or leaders of the churchesINDENT7--<b>4)</b> used of any kind of leader, chief, commanderINDENT7--<b>5)</b> the leader in speech, chief, spokesmanINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to consider, deem, account, think<BR> <!--For Synonyms see entry 5837<br />--><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἡγέομαι h&#x113;g&#xE9;omai, hayg-eh&#39;-om-ahee; middle voice of a (presumed) strengthened form of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=71&page=1\">G71</a>; to lead, i.e. command (with official authority); figuratively, to deem, i.e. consider:&#8212;account, (be) chief, count, esteem, governor, judge, have the rule over, suppose, think.";
