Lex["2240"] = "heko {hay'-ko}|AV - come 27; 27|a primary verb|TDNT - 2:926,306|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to have come, have arrived, be presentINDENT0--<b>2)</b> metaph.INDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to come to one, i.e. to seek an intimacy with one, become his follower: to come upon one (unexpectedly)INDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to come upon one, of things endured<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἥκω h&#x1E17;k&#x14D;, hay&#39;-ko; a primary verb; to arrive, i.e. be present (literally or figuratively):&#8212;come.";
Lex["2241"] = "eli {ay-lee'}|AV - Eli 2; 2|of Hebrew origin, 0410 with pronominal suffix||noun proper masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani. The Hebrew form, as Elio, Elio, etc., is the Syro-Chaldaic (the common language in use by the Jews in the time of Christ) of the first words of the twenty second Psalm; they mean \"My God, My God, why hast thou forsaken me?\"<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἠλί &#x113;l&#xED;, ay-lee&#39;; of Hebrew origin (Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=H410\">H410</a> with pronominal suffix); my God:&#8212;Eli.";
