Lex["2309"] = "thelo {thel'-o} or ethelo {eth-el'-o} in certain tenses<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;theleo {thel-eh'-o} and etheleo {eth-el-eh'-o} which are<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;otherwise obsolete|AV - will/would 159, will/would have 16, desire 13, desirous 3,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;list 3, to will 2, misc 4; 210|apparently strengthened from the alternate form of 138|TDNT - 3:44,318|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to will, have in mind, intend<BR>INDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to be resolved or determined, to purposeINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to desire, to wishINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> to loveINDENT7--<b>1)</b> to like to do a thing, be fond of doingINDENT3-- <b>d)</b> to take delight in, have pleasure<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>θέλω th&#xE9;l&#x14D;, thel&#39;-o; apparently strengthened from the alternate form of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=138&page=1\">G138</a>; to determine (as an active option from subjective impulse; whereas Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1014&page=1\">G1014</a> properly denotes rather a passive acquiescence in objective considerations), i.e. choose or prefer (literally or figuratively); by implication, to wish, i.e. be inclined to (sometimes adverbially, gladly); impersonally for the future tense, to be about to; by Hebraism, to delight in:&#8212;desire, be disposed (forward), intend, list, love, mean, please, have rather, (be) will (have, -ling, - ling(-ly)).";
