Lex["2358"] = "thriambeuo {three-am-byoo'-o}|AV - cause to triumph 1, triumph over 1; 2|from a prolonged compound of the base of 2360|TDNT - 3:159,337|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to triumph, to celebrate a triumphINDENT0--<b>2)</b> cause one to triumph<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />From the root word meaning a hymn sung in festal processions in honour of the god Bacchus (aka, Dionysus).<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> θριαμβεύω thriambe&#xFA;&#x14D;, three-am-byoo&#39;-o; from a prolonged compound of the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2360&page=1\">G2360</a>; and a derivative of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=680&page=1\">G680</a> (meaning a noisy iambus, sung in honor of Bacchus); to make an acclamatory procession, i.e. (figuratively) to conquer or (by Hebraism) to give victory:&#8212;(cause) to triumph (over).";
