Lex["2393"] = "iaspis {ee'-as-pis}|AV - jasper 4; 4|probably of foreign origin, see 03471||noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> jasper, a precious stone of various colours (for some are purple, others blue, others green, and others the colour of brass)<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />There is one kind called the \'Aeizusa\', like to air and another \'Crystallizusa\', clear as crystal. So Pliny speaks of a white \'jasper\' called \'Astrios\', and which, he says is <i>crystallo propinquans</i>, \'near to crystal\', found in India, and on the shores of Pallene. (John Gill&ndash;Comments on Revelation 21:11)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ἴασπις &#xED;aspis, ee&#39;-as-pis; probably of foreign origin (see Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=H3471\">H3471</a>); \"jasper\", a gem:&#8212;jasper.";
