Lex["2588"] = "kardia {kar-dee'-ah}|AV - heart 159, broken hearted + 4937 1; 160|prolonged from a primary kar (Latin, cor, \"heart\")|TDNT - 3:605,415|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the heartINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> that organ in the animal body which is the centre of the circulation of the blood, and hence was regarded as the seat of physical lifeINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> denotes the centre of all physical and spiritual lifeINDENT7--<b>1)</b> the vigour and sense of physical lifeINDENT7--<b>2)</b> the centre and seat of spiritual lifeINDENT12-- <b>a)</b> the soul or mind, as it is the fountain and seat of the thoughts, passions, desires, appetites, affections, purposes, endeavoursINDENT12-- <b>b)</b> of the understanding, the faculty and seat of the intelligenceINDENT12-- <b>c)</b> of the will and characterINDENT12-- <b>d)</b> of the soul so far as it is affected and stirred in a bad way or good, or of the soul as the seat of the sensibilities, affections, emotions, desires, appetites, passionsINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> of the middle or central or inmost part of anything, even though inanimate<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> καρδία kard&#xED;a, kar-dee&#39;-ah; prolonged from a primary &#x3BA;&#x1F71;&#x3C1; k&#xE1;r (Latin cor, \"heart\"); the heart, i.e. (figuratively) the thoughts or feelings (mind); also (by analogy) the middle:&#8212;(<sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><b>X</b></span></a></sup>broken-)heart(-ed).";
