Lex["2853"] = "kollao {kol-lah'-o}|AV - join (one's) self 4, cleave 3, be joined 2, keep company 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;vr reach 1; 11|from kolla (\"glue\")|TDNT - 3:822,452|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to glue, to glue together, cement, fasten togetherINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to join or fasten firmly togetherINDENT0--<b>3)</b> to join one's self to, cleave to<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> κολλάω koll&#xE1;&#x14D;, kol-lah&#39;-o; from &#x3BA;&#x1F79;&#x3BB;&#x3BB;&#x3B1; k&#xF3;lla ( \"glue\"); to glue, i.e. (passively or reflexively) to stick (figuratively):&#8212;cleave, join (self), keep company.";
Lex["2854"] = "kollourion {kol-loo'-ree-on}|AV - eyesalve 1; 1|from a presumed derivative of kollura (a cake - prob akin to the base of 2853)||noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a preparation composed of various materials and used as a remedy for tender eyelids<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>κολλούριον kollo&#xFA;rion, kol-loo&#39;-ree-on; neuter of a presumed derivative of &#x3BA;&#x3BF;&#x3BB;&#x3BB;&#x1F7B;&#x3C1;&#x3B1; koll&#xFD;ra (a cake; prob akin to the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2853&page=1\">G2853</a>); properly, a poultice (as made of or in the form of crackers), i.e. (by analogy) a plaster:&#8212;eyesalve.";
