Lex["2889"] = "kosmos {kos'-mos}|AV - world 186, adorning 1; 187|probably from the base of 2865|TDNT - 3:868,459|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> an apt and harmonious arrangement or constitution, order, governmentINDENT0--<b>2)</b> ornament, decoration, adornment, i.e. the arrangement of the stars,<BR> 'the heavenly hosts', as the ornament of the heavens. 1 Pet. 3:3INDENT0--<b>3)</b> the world, the universeINDENT0--<b>4)</b> the circle of the earth, the earthINDENT0--<b>5)</b> the inhabitants of the earth, men, the human familyINDENT0--<b>6)</b> the ungodly multitude; the whole mass of men alienated from God, and therefore hostile to the cause of ChristINDENT0--<b>7)</b> world affairs, the aggregate of things earthlyINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> the whole circle of earthly goods, endowments riches, advantages, pleasures, etc, which although hollow and frail and fleeting, stir desire, seduce from God and are obstacles to the cause of ChristINDENT0--<b>8)</b> any aggregate or general collection of particulars of any sortINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> the Gentiles as contrasted to the Jews (Rom. 11:12 etc)INDENT3-- <b>b)</b> of believers only, John 1:29; 3:16; 3:17; 6:33; 12:47 1 Cor. 4:9; 2 Cor. 5:19<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> κόσμος k&#xF3;smos, kos&#39;-mos; probably from the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2865&page=1\">G2865</a>; orderly arrangement, i.e. decoration; by implication, the world (in a wide or narrow sense, including its inhabitants, literally or figuratively (morally)):&#8212;adorning, world.";
Lex["2890"] = "Kouartos {koo'-ar-tos}|AV - Quartus 1; 1|of Latin origin (fourth)||noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Quartus = \"fourth\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a Roman; probably before he lived at Rome, and therefore sends his salutations to the Christians there: he is mentioned among the seventy disciples, and said to be bishop of Berytus. (Gill)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Κούαρτος Ko&#xFA;artos, koo&#39;-ar-tos; of Latin origin (fourth); Quartus, a Christian:&#8212;Quartus.";
