Lex["2892"] = "koustodia {koos-to-dee'-ah}|AV - watch 3; 3|of Latin origin||noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> guard: used of Roman soldiers guarding the sepulchre of Christ<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />A Roman guard was made up of four to sixteen solders. In combat, they would form a square, and were able to hold off a much larger force.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> κουστωδία koust&#x14D;d&#xED;a, koos-to-dee&#39;-ah; of Latin origin; \"custody\", i.e. a Roman sentry:&#8212;watch.";
