Lex["2936"] = "ktizo {ktid'-zo}|AV - create 12, Creator 1, make 1; 14|probably akin to 2932 (through the idea of proprietor-ship of the manufacturer)|TDNT - 3:1000,481|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to make habitable, to people, a place, region, islandINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to found a city, colony, stateINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to createINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of God creating the worldsINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to form, shape, i.e. to completely change or transform<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> κτίζω kt&#xED;z&#x14D;, ktid&#39;-zo; probably akin to Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2932&page=1\">G2932</a> (through the idea of proprietorship of the manufacturer); to fabricate, i.e. found (form originally):&#8212;create, Creator, make.";
Lex["2937"] = "ktisis {ktis'-is}|AV - creature 11, creation 6, building 1, ordinance 1; 19|from 2936|TDNT - 3:1000,481|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the act of founding, establishing, building etcINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> the act of creating, creationINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> creation i.e. thing createdINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of individual things, beings, a creature, a creation<BR>INDENT12-- <b>a)</b> anything createdINDENT12-- <b>b)</b> after a rabbinical usage (by which a man converted from idolatry to Judaism was called)INDENT12-- <b>c)</b> the sum or aggregate of things createdINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> institution, ordinance<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> κτίσις kt&#xED;sis, ktis&#39;-is; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2936&page=1\">G2936</a>; original formation (properly, the act; by implication, the thing, literally or figuratively):&#8212;building, creation, creature, ordinance.";
