Lex["3434"] = "Moloch {mol-okh'}|AV - Moloch 1; 1|of Hebrew origin 04432||noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Molech = \"king\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the name of the idol god of the Ammonites, to which human victims, particularly young children were offered in sacrifice. Its image was a hollow brazen figure, with the head of an ox, and outstretched human arms. It was heated red hot by a fire from within, and the little ones placed in its arms to be slowly burned, while to prevent the parents from hearing the dying cries, the sacrificing priests beat drums<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Μολόχ Mol&#xF3;ch, mol-okh&#39;; of Hebrew origin (Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=H4432\">H4432</a>); Moloch (i.e. Molek), an idol:&#8212;Moloch.";
