Lex["3700"] = "optanomai {op-tan'-om-ahee} or optomai {op-tom-ahee}|AV - see 37, appear 17, look 2, show (one's) self 1, being seen 1; 58|a (middle voice) prolonged form of the primary (middle voice) optomai {op'-tom-ahee}, which is used for it in certain tenses, and both as alternate of 3708|TDNT - 5:315,706|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to look at, beholdINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to allow one's self to be seen, to appear<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ὀπτάνομαι opt&#xE1;nomai, op-tan&#39;-om-ahee; a (middle voice) prolonged form of the primary (middle voice) &#x1F44;&#x3C0;&#x3C4;&#x3BF;&#x3BC;&#x3B1;&#x3B9; &#xF3;ptomai op&#39;-tom-ahee; which is used for it in certain tenses; and both as alternate of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3708&page=1\">G3708</a>; to gaze (i.e. with wide-open eyes, as at something remarkable; and thus differing from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=991&page=1\">G991</a>, which denotes simply voluntary observation; and from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1492&page=1\">G1492</a>, which expresses merely mechanical, passive or casual vision; while Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2300&page=1\">G2300</a>, and still more emphatically its intensive Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2334&page=1\">G2334</a>, signifies an earnest but more continued inspection; and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4648&page=1\">G4648</a> a watching from a distance):&#8212;appear, look, see, shew self.";
