Lex["3819"] = "palai {pal'-ahee}|AV - long ago 1, any while 1, a great while ago 1, old 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;in time past 1, of old 1; 6|probably another form for 3825 (through the idea of retrocession)|TDNT - 5:717,769|adverb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> of old, formerINDENT0--<b>2)</b> long ago<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πάλαι p&#xE1;lai, pal&#39;-ahee; probably another form for Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3825&page=1\">G3825</a> (through the idea of retrocession); (adverbially) formerly, or (by relatively) sometime since; (elliptically as adjective) ancient:&#8212;any while, a great while ago, (of) old, in time past.";
Lex["3820"] = "palaios {pal-ah-yos'}|AV - old 18, old wine 1; 19|from 3819|TDNT - 5:717,769|adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> old, ancientINDENT0--<b>2)</b> no longer new, worn by use, the worse for wear, old<BR> <!--For Synonyms see entry 5816<br />--><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> παλαιός palai&#xF3;s, pal-ah-yos&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3819&page=1\">G3819</a>; antique, i.e. not recent, worn out:&#8212;old.";
