Lex["3962"] = "pater {pat-ayr'}|AV - Father 268, father 150; 419|apparently a root word|TDNT - 5:945,805|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> generator or male ancestorINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> either the nearest ancestor: father of the corporeal nature, natural fathers, both parentsINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> a more remote ancestor, the founder of a family or tribe, progenitor of a people, forefather: so Abraham is called, Jacob and DavidINDENT7--<b>1)</b> fathers i.e. ancestors, forefathers, founders of a nationINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> one advanced in years, a seniorINDENT0--<b>2)</b> metaph.INDENT3-- <b>a)</b> the originator and transmitter of anythingINDENT7--<b>1)</b> the authors of a family or society of persons animated by the same spirit as himselfINDENT7--<b>2)</b> one who has infused his own spirit into others, who actuates and governs their mindsINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> one who stands in a father's place and looks after another in a paternal wayINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> a title of honourINDENT7--<b>1)</b> teachers, as those to whom pupils trace back the knowledge and training they have receivedINDENT7--<b>2)</b> the members of the Sanhedrin, whose prerogative it was by virtue of the wisdom and experience in which they excelled, to take charge of the interests of othersINDENT0--<b>3)</b> God is called the FatherINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of the stars, the heavenly luminaries, because he is their creator, upholder, rulerINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> of all rational and intelligent beings, whether angels or men, because he is their creator, preserver, guardian and protectorINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of spiritual beings and of all menINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> of Christians, as those who through Christ have been exalted to a specially close and intimate relationship with God, and who no longer dread him as a stern judge of sinners, but revere him as their reconciled and loving FatherINDENT3-- <b>d)</b> the Father of Jesus Christ, as one whom God has united to himself in the closest bond of love and intimacy, made acquainted with his purposes, appointed to explain and carry out among men the plan of salvation, and made to share also in his own divine natureINDENT7--<b>1)</b> by Jesus Christ himselfINDENT7--<b>2)</b> by the apostles<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>πατήρ pat&#x1E17;r, pat-ayr&#39;; apparently a primary word; a \"father\" (literally or figuratively, near or more remote):&#8212;father, parent.";
