Lex["4138"] = "pleroma {play'-ro-mah}|AV - fulness 13, full 1, fulfilling 1, which is put in to fill up 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;pierce that filled up 1; 17|from 4137|TDNT - 6:298,867|noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> that which is (has been) filledINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> a ship inasmuch as it is filled (i.e. manned) with sailors,<BR> rowers, and soldiersINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> in the NT, the body of believers, as that which is filled with the presence, power, agency, riches of God and of ChristINDENT0--<b>2)</b> that which fills or with which a thing is filledINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of those things which a ship is filled, freight and merchandise, sailors, oarsmen, soldiersINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> completeness or fulness of timeINDENT0--<b>3)</b> fulness, abundanceINDENT0--<b>4)</b> a fulfilling, keeping<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πλήρωμα pl&#x1E17;r&#x14D;ma, play&#39;-ro-mah; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4137&page=1\">G4137</a>; repletion or completion, i.e. (subjectively) what fills (as contents, supplement, copiousness, multitude), or (objectively) what is filled (as container, performance, period):&#8212;which is put in to fill up, piece that filled up, fulfilling, full, fulness.";
