Lex["4151"] = "pneuma {pnyoo'-mah}|AV - Spirit 111, Holy Ghost 89, Spirit (of God) 13,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Spirit (of the Lord) 5, (My) Spirit 3, Spirit (of truth) 3,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Spirit (of Christ) 2, human (spirit) 49, (evil) spirit 47,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;spirit (general) 26, spirit 8, (Jesus' own) spirit 6,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(Jesus' own) ghost 2, misc 21; 385|from 4154|TDNT - 6:332,876|noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the third person of the triune God, the Holy Spirit, coequal, coeternal with the Father and the SonINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> sometimes referred to in a way which emphasises his personality and character (the \"Holy\" Spirit)INDENT3-- <b>b)</b> sometimes referred to in a way which emphasises his work and power (the Spirit of \"Truth\")INDENT3-- <b>c)</b> never referred to as a depersonalised forceINDENT0--<b>2)</b> the spirit, i.e. the vital principal by which the body is animatedINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> the rational spirit, the power by which the human being feels, thinks, decidesINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> the soulINDENT0--<b>3)</b> a spirit, i.e. a simple essence, devoid of all or at least all grosser matter, and possessed of the power of knowing, desiring, deciding, and actingINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> a life giving spiritINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> a human soul that has left the bodyINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> a spirit higher than man but lower than God, i.e. an angelINDENT7--<b>1)</b> used of demons, or evil spirits, who were conceived as inhabiting the bodies of men<BR>INDENT7--<b>2)</b> the spiritual nature of Christ, higher than the highest angels and equal to God, the divine nature of ChristINDENT0--<b>4)</b> the disposition or influence which fills and governs the soul of any oneINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> the efficient source of any power, affection, emotion, desire, etc.INDENT0--<b>5)</b> a movement of air (a gentle blast)INDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of the wind, hence the wind itselfINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> breath of nostrils or mouth<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πνεῦμα pne&#xFB;ma, pnyoo&#39;-mah; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4154&page=1\">G4154</a>; a current of air, i.e. breath (blast) or a breeze; by analogy or figuratively, a spirit, i.e. (human) the rational soul, (by implication) vital principle, mental disposition, etc., or (superhuman) an angel, demon, or (divine) God, Christ&#39;s spirit, the Holy Spirit:&#8212;ghost, life, spirit(-ual, -ually), mind. Compare Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5590&page=1\">G5590</a>.";
Lex["4152"] = "pneumatikos {pnyoo-mat-ik-os'}|AV - spiritual 26; 26|from 4151|TDNT - 6:332,876|adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> relating to the human spirit, or rational soul, as part of the man which is akin to God and serves as his instrument or organINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> that which possesses the nature of the rational soulINDENT0--<b>2)</b> belonging to a spirit, or a being higher than man but inferior to GodINDENT0--<b>3)</b> belonging to the Divine SpiritINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of God the Holy SpiritINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> one who is filled with and governed by the Spirit of GodINDENT0--<b>4)</b> pertaining to the wind or breath; windy, exposed to the wind, blowing<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πνευματικός pneumatik&#xF3;s, pnyoo-mat-ik-os&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4151&page=1\">G4151</a>; non-carnal, i.e. (humanly) ethereal (as opposed to gross), or (dæmoniacally) a spirit (concretely), or (divinely) supernatural, regenerate, religious:&#8212;spiritual. Compare Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5591&page=1\">G5591</a>.";
Lex["4153"] = "pneumatikos {pnyoo-mat-ik-oce'}|AV - spiritual 2; 2|from 4152||adverb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> spiritually: i.e. by the aid of the Holy Spirit<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πνευματικῶς pneumatik&#x14D;s, pnyoo-mat-ik-oce&#39;; adverb from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4152&page=1\">G4152</a>; non-physically, i.e. divinely, figuratively:&#8212;spiritually.";
