Lex["4190"] = "poneros {pon-ay-ros'}|AV - evil 51, wicked 10, wicked one 6, evil things 2, misc 7; 76|from a derivative of 4192|TDNT - 6:546,912|adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> full of labours, annoyances, hardshipsINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> pressed and harassed by laboursINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> bringing toils, annoyances, perils; of a time full of peril to Christian faith and steadfastness; causing pain and troubleINDENT0--<b>2)</b> bad, of a bad nature or conditionINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> in a physical sense: diseased or blindINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> in an ethical sense: evil wicked, bad<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />Referring to Mat 6:13: \"Although the KJV renders this \'deliver us from evil,\' the presence of the article indicates not evil in general, but the evil one himself. In the context of Matthew\'s Gospel, such deliverance from the devil seems to be linked to Jesus\' temptation in Mat 4:1-10: Because the Spirit led him into temptation by the evil one, believers now participate in his victory\" (Daniel B. Wallace, <i>Greek Grammar Beyond the Basics</i>, p. 233).<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πονηρός pon&#x113;r&#xF3;s, pon-ay-ros&#39;; from a derivative of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4192&page=1\">G4192</a>; hurtful, i.e. evil (properly, in effect or influence, and thus differing from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2556&page=1\">G2556</a>, which refers rather to essential character, as well as from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4550&page=1\">G4550</a>, which indicates degeneracy from original virtue); figuratively, calamitous; also (passively) ill, i.e. diseased; but especially (morally) culpable, i.e. derelict, vicious, facinorous; neuter (singular) mischief, malice, or (plural) guilt; masculine (singular) the devil, or (plural) sinners:&#8212;bad, evil, grievous, harm, lewd, malicious, wicked(-ness). See also Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4191&page=1\">G4191</a>.";
Lex["4191"] = "poneroteros {pon-ay-rot'-er-os}|AV - more wicked 2; 2|comparative of 4190||adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> more evil<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πονηρότερος pon&#x113;r&#xF3;teros, pon-ay-rot&#39;-er-os; comparative of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4190&page=1\">G4190</a>; more evil:&#8212;more wicked.";
