Lex["4314"] = "pros {pros}|AV - unto 340, to 203, with 43, for 25, against 24, among 20, at 11,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;not tr 6, misc 53, vr to 1; 726|a strengthened form of 4253|TDNT - 6:720,942|prep|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to the advantage ofINDENT0--<b>2)</b> at, near, byINDENT0--<b>3)</b> to, towards, with, with regard to<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πρός pr&#xF3;s, pros; a strengthened form of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4253&page=1\">G4253</a>; a preposition of direction; forward to, i.e. toward (with the genitive case, the side of, i.e. pertaining to; with the dative case, by the side of, i.e. near to; usually with the accusative case, the place, time, occasion, or respect, which is the destination of the relation, i.e. whither or for which it is predicated):&#8212;about, according to , against, among, at, because of, before, between, (where-)by, for, <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><b>X</b></a></sup>at thy house, in, for intent, nigh unto, of, which pertain to, that, to (the end that), <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><b>X</b></a></sup>together, to (you) -ward, unto, with(-in). In the comparative case, it denotes essentially the same applications, namely, motion towards, accession to, or nearness at.";
