Lex["4394"] = "propheteia {prof-ay-ti'-ah}|AV - prophecy 16, prophesying 3; 19|from 4396 (\"prophecy\")|TDNT - 6:781,952|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> prophecyINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> a discourse emanating from divine inspiration and declaring the purposes of God, whether by reproving and admonishing the wicked, or comforting the afflicted, or revealing things hidden; esp. by foretelling future eventsINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> Used in the NT of the utterance of OT prophetsINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of the prediction of events relating to Christ's kingdom and its speedy triumph, together with the consolations and admonitions pertaining to it, the spirit of prophecy, the divine mind, to which the prophetic faculty is dueINDENT7--<b>2)</b> of the endowment and speech of the Christian teachers called prophetsINDENT7--<b>3)</b> the gifts and utterances of these prophets, esp. of the predictions of the works of which, set apart to teach the gospel, will accomplish for the kingdom of Christ<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> προφητεία proph&#x113;te&#xED;a, prof-ay-ti&#39;-ah; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4396&page=1\">G4396</a> ( \"prophecy\"); prediction (scriptural or other):&#8212;prophecy, prophesying.";
