Lex["4456"] = "poroo {po-ro'-o}|AV - harden 3, blind 2; 5|apparently from poros (a kind of stone)|TDNT - 5:1025,816|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to cover with a thick skin, to harden by covering with a callusINDENT0--<b>2)</b> metaph.INDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to make the heart dullINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to grow hard, callous, become dull, lose the power of understanding<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πωρόω p&#x14D;r&#xF3;&#x14D;, po-ro&#39;-o; apparently from &#x3C0;&#x1FF6;&#x3C1;&#x3BF;&#x3C2; p&#x14D;ros (a kind of stone); to petrify, i.e. (figuratively) to indurate (render stupid or callous):&#8212;blind, harden.";
Lex["4457"] = "porosis {po'-ro-sis}|AV - blindness 2, hardness 1; 3|from 4456|TDNT - 5:1025,816|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the covering with a callusINDENT0--<b>2)</b> obtrusiveness of mental discernment, dulled perceptionINDENT0--<b>3)</b> the mind of one has been bluntedINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of stubbornness, obduracy<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πώρωσις p&#x1E53;r&#x14D;sis, po&#39;-ro-sis; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4456&page=1\">G4456</a>; stupidity or callousness:&#8212;blindness, hardness.";
Lex["4458"] = "-pos {poce}|AV - be any means 6, by some means 1, perhaps 1, haply 1, not tr 5; 14|adverb from the base of 4225, an enclitic particle of indefiniteness of manner||particle|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> by any means, at all, perhaps<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> -πώς -p&#x1E53;s, poce; adverb from the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4225&page=1\">G4225</a>; an enclitic particle of indefiniteness of manner; somehow or anyhow; used only in composition:&#8212;haply, by any (some) means, perhaps. See Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1513&page=1\">G1513</a>, Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3381&page=1\">G3381</a>. Compare Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4459&page=1\">G4459</a>.";
Lex["4459"] = "pos {poce}|AV - how 99, by what means 2, after what manner 1, that 1; 103|adverb from the base of 4226, an interrogative particle of manner||particle|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> how, in what way<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> πῶς p&#x14D;s, poce; adverb from the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4226&page=1\">G4226</a>; an interrogative particle of manner; in what way? (sometimes the question is indirect, how?); also as exclamation, how much!:&#8212;how, after (by) what manner (means), that. (Occasionally unexpressed in English).";
