Lex["4486"] = "rhegnumi {hrayg'-noo-mee} or rhesso {hrace'-so}|AV - burst 2, tear 1, rend 1, break 1, break forth 1, throw down 1; 7|both prolonged forms of rheko (which appears only in certain forms, and is itself probably a strengthened form of agnumi [see in 2608])||verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to rend, burst or break asunder, break up, break throughINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to tear in piecesINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to break forthINDENT7--<b>1)</b> into joy, of infants or dumb persons beginning to speakINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> to distort, convulseINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of a demon causing convulsions in a man possessedINDENT7--<b>2)</b> to dash down, hurl to the ground (a common occurrence in cases of demon possession and epilepsy)<BR> <!--For Synonyms see entry 5850<br />--><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ῥήγνυμι rh&#x1E17;gnymi, hrayg&#39;-noo-mee; both prolonged forms of &#x1FE5;&#x1F75;&#x3BA;&#x3C9; rh&#x1E17;k&#x14D; (which appears only in certain forms, and is itself probably a strengthened form of &#x1F04;&#x3B3;&#x3BD;&#x3C5;&#x3BC;&#x3B9; &#xE1;gnymi (see in Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2608&page=1\">G2608</a>)) to  \"break,\" \"wreck\" or \"crack\", i.e. (especially) to sunder (by separation of the parts; Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2608&page=1\">G2608</a> being its intensive (with the preposition in composition), and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2352&page=1\">G2352</a> a shattering to minute fragments; but not a reduction to the constituent particles, like Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3089&page=1\">G3089</a>) or disrupt, lacerate; by implication, to convulse (with spasms); figuratively, to give vent to joyful emotions:&#8212;break (forth), burst, rend, tear.";
