Lex["4611"] = "Siloam {sil-o-am'}|AV - Siloam 3; 3|of Hebrew origin 07975||noun proper location| INDENT0--Siloam = \"sent\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the Pool of Siloam, a fountain of water in Jerusalem, also called Shiloah in Isa. 8:6INDENT0--<b>2)</b> the Tower of Siloam, may have been a tower near or over the Pool of Siloam, which fell down killing 18 men; very likely they were purifying themselves. (Gill)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Σιλωάμ Sil&#x14D;&#xE1;m, sil-o-am&#39;; of Hebrew origin (Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_hebrew.html?strongs=H7975\">H7975</a>); Siloam (i.e. Shiloach), a pool of Jerusalem:&#8212;Siloam.";
