Lex["4697"] = "splagchnizomai {splangkh-nid'-zom-ahee}|AV - have compassion 7, be moved with compassion 5; 12|middle voice from 4698|TDNT - 7:548,1067|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to be moved as to one's bowels, hence to be moved with compassion, have compassion (for the bowels were thought to be the seat of love and pity)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> σπλαγχνίζομαι splanchn&#xED;zomai, splangkh-nid&#39;-zom-ahee; middle voice from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4698&page=1\">G4698</a>; to have the bowels yearn, i.e. (figuratively) feel sympathy, to pity:&#8212;have (be moved with) compassion.";
Lex["4698"] = "splagchnon {splangkh'-non}|AV - bowels 9, inward affection 1, tender mercy + 1656 1; 11|probably strengthened from splen (the \"spleen\")|TDNT - 7:548,1067|noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> bowels, intestines, (the heart, lungs, liver, etc.)INDENT3-- <b>a)</b> bowelsINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> the bowels were regarded as the seat of the more violent passions, such as anger and love; but by the Hebrews as the seat of the tenderer affections, esp. kindness, benevolence, compassion; hence our heart (tender mercies, affections, etc.)INDENT3-- <b>c)</b> a heart in which mercy resides<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> σπλάγχνον spl&#xE1;nchnon, splangkh&#39;-non; probably strengthened from &#x3C3;&#x3C0;&#x3BB;&#x1F75;&#x3BD; spl&#x1E17;n (the \"spleen\"); an intestine (plural); figuratively, pity or sympathy:&#8212;bowels, inward affection, <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><b>X</b></span></a></sup>tender mercy.";
