Lex["4810"] = "sukon {soo'-kon}|AV - fig 4; 4|apparently a primary word|TDNT - 7:751,1100|noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a fig, the ripe fruit of a fig tree<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> σῦκον s&#x177;kon, soo&#39;-kon; apparently a primary word; a fig:&#8212;fig.";
Lex["4811"] = "sukophanteo {soo-kof-an-teh'-o}|AV - accuse falsely 1, take by false accusation 1; 2|from a compound of 4810 and a derivative of 5316|TDNT - 7:759,1100|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to accuse wrongfully, to calumniate, to attack by malicious devicesINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to exact money wrongfullyINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to extort from, defraud<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />\"From <i>sykon phainein</i>, orig. used of denouncers of the attempted export of figs from Athens, acc. to Ister 35, Plu. Sol. 24, 2.523b; orig. of citizens entrusted with the collection of figs as part of the public revenues of Athens and the denouncing of tax-evaders, acc. to Philomnest.1; of denouncers of figs which had been stolen from the sacred fig-trees during a famine and had become cheap, the famine having passed, Sch. Ar. Pl. 31, cf. Fest. p.393 L.; these and modern explanations are mere guesses; the word first in Ar. but implied by <i>sykopedilos</i>.\" (Liddel-Scott-Jones, <i>A Greek-English Lexicon</i>)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> συκοφαντέω sykophant&#xE9;&#x14D;, soo-kof-an-teh&#39;-o; from a compound of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4810&page=1\">G4810</a> and a derivative of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5316&page=1\">G5316</a>; to be a fig-informer (reporter of the law forbidding the exportation of figs from Greece), \"sycophant\", i.e. (genitive and by extension) to defraud (exact unlawfully, extort):&#8212;accuse falsely, take by false accusation.";
Lex["4812"] = "sulagogeo {soo-lag-ogue-eh'-o}|AV - spoil 1; 1|from the base of 4813 and (the reduplicated form of) 71||verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to carry off bootyINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to carry one off as a captive (and slave)INDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to lead away from the truth and subject to one's sway<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> συλαγωγέω sylag&#x14D;g&#xE9;&#x14D;, soo-lag-ogue-eh&#39;-o; from the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4813&page=1\">G4813</a> and (the reduplicated form of) Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=71&page=1\">G71</a>; to lead away as booty, i.e. (figuratively) seduce:&#8212;spoil.";
