Lex["4861"] = "sumpsuchos {soom'-psoo-khos}|AV - of one accord 1; 1|from 4862 and 5590||adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> of one mind, of one accord<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />This word is made up of two words <i>syn</i> (together with) and <i>psychos</i> (soul, self, inner life, or the seat of the feelings, desires, affections). So the word refers to being \'united in spirit\' or harmonious (BDAG). Paul desired the Philippians to be united in their affections&ndash;one in Christ in all desires! Phl 2:2 is the only occurrence of this word in the NT. (Wayne Steury)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> σύμψυχος s&#xFD;mpsychos, soom&#39;-psoo-khos; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4862&page=1\">G4862</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5590&page=1\">G5590</a>; co-spirited, i.e. similar in sentiment:&#8212;like-minded.";
Lex["4862"] = "sun {soon}|AV - with 123, beside 1, accompany + 2064 1; 125|a primary preposition denoting union|TDNT - 7:766,1102|prep|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> with<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> σύν s&#xFD;n, soon; a primary preposition denoting union; with or together (but much closer than Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3326&page=1\">G3326</a> or Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3844&page=1\">G3844</a>), i.e. by association, companionship, process, resemblance, possession, instrumentality, addition, etc.:&#8212;beside, with. In composition it has similar applications, including completeness.";
Lex["4863"] = "sunago {soon-ag'-o}|AV - gather 15, be gathered together 12, gather together 9,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;come together 6, be gathered 4, be assembled 3, take in 3,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;misc 10; 62|from 4862 and 71||verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to gather together, to gatherINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to draw together, collectINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of fishesINDENT7--<b>2)</b> of a net in which they are caughtINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to bring together, assemble, collectINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to join together, join in one (those previously separated)INDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to gather together by convokingINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> to be gathered i.e. come together, gather, meetINDENT0--<b>3)</b> to lead with one's selfINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> into one's home, i.e. to receive hospitably, to entertain<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> συνάγω syn&#xE1;g&#x14D;, soon-ag&#39;-o; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4862&page=1\">G4862</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=71&page=1\">G71</a>; to lead together, i.e. collect or convene; specially, to entertain (hospitably):&#8212;<sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><b>X</b></span></a></sup>accompany, assemble (selves, together), bestow, come together, gather (selves together, up, together), lead into, resort, take in.";
Lex["4864"] = "sunagoge {soon-ag-o-gay'}|AV - synagogue 55, congregation 1, assembly 1; 57|from (the reduplicated form of) 4863|TDNT - 7:798,1108|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a bringing together, gathering (as of fruits), a contractingINDENT0--<b>2)</b> in the NT, an assembling together of men, an assembly of menINDENT0--<b>3)</b> a synagogueINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> an assembly of Jews formally gathered together to offer prayers and listen to the reading and expositions of the scriptures; assemblies of that sort were held every sabbath and feast day, afterwards also on the second and fifth days of every week; name transferred to an assembly of Christians formally gathered together for religious purposesINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> the buildings where those solemn Jewish assemblies are held. Synagogues seem to date their origin from the Babylonian exile. In the times of Jesus and the apostles every town, not only in Palestine, but also among the Gentiles if it contained a considerable number of Jewish inhabitants, had at least one synagogue, the larger towns several or even many. These were also used for trials and inflicting punishment.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> συναγωγή synag&#x14D;g&#x1E17;, soon-ag-o-gay&#39;; from (the reduplicated form of) Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4863&page=1\">G4863</a>; an assemblage of persons; specially, a Jewish \"synagogue\" (the meeting or the place); by analogy, a Christian church:&#8212;assembly, congregation, synagogue.";
Lex["4865"] = "sunagonizomai {soon-ag-o-nid'-zom-ahee}|AV - strive together with 1; 1|from 4862 and 75||verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to strive together with one, to help one in striving<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> συναγωνίζομαι synag&#x14D;n&#xED;zomai, soon-ag-o-nid&#39;-zom-ahee; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4862&page=1\">G4862</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=75&page=1\">G75</a>; to struggle in company with, i.e. (figuratively) to be a partner (assistant):&#8212;strive together with.";
