Lex["4990"] = "soter {so-tare'}|AV - Saviour 24; 24|from 4982|TDNT - 7:1003,1132|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> saviour, deliverer, preserver<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />The name was given by the ancients to deities, esp. tutelary deities, to princes, kings, and in general to men who had conferred signal benefits upon their country, and in more degenerate days by the way of flattery to personages of influence (Wigram). The word <i>soter</i> was a common Greek epithet for the gods (e.g., Zeus, Apollo, and Hermes), active personalities in world affairs (e.g., Epicurus) and rulers (e.g., Ptolemy Philopator, and later Roman Emporers). (cf. LSJ and BDAG)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> σωτήρ s&#x14D;t&#x1E17;r, so-tare&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4982&page=1\">G4982</a>; a deliverer, i.e. God or Christ:&#8212;saviour.";
Lex["4991"] = "soteria {so-tay-ree'-ah}|AV - salvation 40, the (one) be saved 1, deliver + 1325 1, health 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;saving 1, that (one) be saved + 1519 1; 45|feminine of a derivative of 4990 as (properly, abstract) noun|TDNT - 7:965,1132|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> deliverance, preservation, safety, salvationINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> deliverance from the molestation of enemiesINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> in an ethical sense, that which concludes to the soul's safety or salvationINDENT7--<b>(1)</b> of Messianic salvationINDENT0--<b>2)</b> salvation as the present possession of all true ChristiansINDENT0--<b>3)</b> future salvation, the sum of benefits and blessings which the Christians, redeemed from all earthly ills, will enjoy after the visible return of Christ from heaven in the consummated and eternal kingdom of God.<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />Scripture describes a fourfold salvation: saved from the penalty, power, presence and most importantly the pleasure of sin.(cf. Arthur W. Pink, <i>A Fourfold Salvation</i>)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> σωτηρία s&#x14D;t&#x113;r&#xED;a, so-tay-ree&#39;-ah; feminine of a derivative of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4990&page=1\">G4990</a> as (properly, abstract) noun; rescue or safety (physically or morally):&#8212;deliver, health, salvation, save, saving.";
Lex["4992"] = "soterion {so-tay'-ree-on}|AV - salvation 4, that brings salvation 1; 5|neuter of the same as 4991 as (properly, concretely) noun|TDNT - 7:1021,1132|adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> saving, bringing salvationINDENT0--<b>2)</b> he who embodies this salvation, or through whom God is about to achieve itINDENT0--<b>3)</b> the hope of (future) salvation<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>σωτήριον s&#x14D;t&#x1E17;rion, so-tay&#39;-ree-on; neuter of the same as Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4991&page=1\">G4991</a> as (properly, concretely) noun; defender or (by implication) defence:&#8212;salvation.";
