Lex["5018"] = "Tarseus {tar-syoos'}|AV - Tarsus 2; 2|from 5019||noun proper masculine| INDENT0--Tarsus = \"a flat basket\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> belong to Tarsus, a native of Tarsus<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Ταρσεύς Tarse&#xFA;s, tar-syoos&#39;; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5019&page=1\">G5019</a>; a Tarsean, i.e. native of Tarsus:&#8212;of Tarsus.";
Lex["5019"] = "Tarsos {tar-sos'}|AV - Tarsus 3; 3|perhaps the same as tarsos (a flat basket)||noun proper location| INDENT0--Tarsus = \"a flat basket\"<BR>INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a major city in Cilicia and the birthplace and early home of Paul. Acts 9:11; 21:39; 22:3. Even in the flourishing period of Greek history it was an important city. In the Roman civil wars, it sided with Caesar and on the occasion of a visit from him its name changed to Juliopolis. Augustus made it a free city. Its was renowned as a place of education under the early Roman emperors. Strabo compares it in this respect to Athens and Alexandria. Tarsus also was a place of much commerce. It was situated in a wild and fertile plain on the banks of the Cydnus. No ruins of any importance remain.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> Ταρσός Tars&#xF3;s, tar-sos&#39;; perhaps the same as &#x3C4;&#x3B1;&#x3C1;&#x3C3;&#x1F79;&#x3C2; tars&#xF3;s (a flat basket); Tarsus, a place in Asia Minor:&#8212;Tarsus.";
Lex["5020"] = "tartaroo {tar-tar-o'-o}|AV - cast down to hell 1; 1|from Tartaros (the deepest abyss of Hell)||verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the name of the subterranean region, doleful and dark, regarded by the ancient Greeks as the abode of the wicked dead, where they suffer punishment for their evil deeds; it answers to Gehenna of the JewsINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to thrust down to Tartarus, to hold captive in Tartarus<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> ταρταρόω tartar&#xF3;&#x14D;, tar-tar-o&#39;-o; from &#x3A4;&#x1F71;&#x3C1;&#x3C4;&#x3B1;&#x3C1;&#x3BF;&#x3C2; T&#xE1;rtaros (the deepest abyss of Hades); to incarcerate in eternal torment:&#8212;cast down to hell.";
Lex["5021"] = "tasso {tas'-so}|AV - appoint 3, ordain 2, set 1, determine 1, addict 1; 8|a prolonged form of a primary verb (which latter appears only in certain tenses)|TDNT - 8:27,1156|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to put in order, to stationINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to place in a certain order, to arrange, to assign a place, to appointINDENT7--<b>1)</b> to assign (appoint) a thing to oneINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to appoint, ordain, orderINDENT7--<b>1)</b> to appoint on one's own responsibility or authorityINDENT7--<b>2)</b> to appoint mutually, i.e. agree upon<BR> <!--For Synonyms see entry 5844<br />--><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τάσσω t&#xE1;ss&#x14D;, tas&#39;-so; a prolonged form of a primary verb (which latter appears only in certain tenses); to arrange in an orderly manner, i.e. assign or dispose (to a certain position or lot):&#8212;addict, appoint, determine, ordain, set.";
