Lex["5043"] = "teknon {tek'-non}|AV - child 77, son 21, daughter 1; 99|from the base of 5098|TDNT - 5:636,759|noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> offspring, childrenINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> childINDENT7--<b>1)</b> a male child, a sonINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> metaph.INDENT7--<b>1)</b> the name transferred to that intimate and reciprocal relationship formed between men by the bonds of love, friendship, trust, just as between parents and childrenINDENT7--<b>2)</b> in affectionate address, such as patrons, helpers, teachers and the like employ: my childINDENT7--<b>3)</b> in the NT, pupils or disciples are called children of their teachers, because the latter by their instruction nourish the minds of their pupils and mould their charactersINDENT7--<b>4)</b> children of God: in the OT of \"the people of Israel\" as especially dear to God, in the NT, in Paul's writings, all who are led by the Spirit of God and thus closely related to GodINDENT7--<b>5)</b> children of the devil: those who in thought and action are prompted by the devil, and so reflect his characterINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> metaph.INDENT7--<b>1)</b> of anything who depends upon it, is possessed by a desire or affection for it, is addicted to itINDENT7--<b>2)</b> one who is liable to any fateINDENT12-- <b>a)</b> thus children of a city: it citizens and inhabitantsINDENT7--<b>3)</b> the votaries of wisdom, those souls who have, as it were, been nurtured and moulded by wisdomINDENT7--<b>4)</b> cursed children, exposed to a curse and doomed to God's wrath or penalty<BR> <!--For Synonyms see entry 5868<br />--><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τέκνον t&#xE9;knon, tek&#39;-non; from the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5098&page=1\">G5098</a>; a child (as produced):&#8212;child, daughter, son.";
