Lex["5055"] = "teleo {tel-eh'-o}|AV - finish 8, fulfil 7, accomplish 4, pay 2, perform 1, expire 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;misc 3; 26|from 5056|TDNT - 8:57,1161|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to bring to a close, to finish, to endINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> passed, finishedINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to perform, execute, complete, fulfil, (so that the thing done corresponds to what has been said, the order, command etc.)INDENT3-- <b>a)</b> with special reference to the subject matter, to carry out the contents of a commandINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> with reference also to the form, to do just as commanded, and generally involving the notion of time, to perform the last act which completes a process, to accomplish, fulfilINDENT0--<b>3)</b> to payINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of tribute<BR /><BR />INDENT0--<b>Additional information from the Outline of Biblical Usage:</b><br />In John 19:30 the word means \"It is finished or paid\" John 19:30. Christ satisfied God\'s justice by dying for all to pay for the sins of the elect. These sins can never be punished again since that would violate God\'s justice. Sins can only be punished once, either by a substitute or by yourself.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τελέω tel&#xE9;&#x14D;, tel-eh&#39;-o; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5056&page=1\">G5056</a>; to end, i.e. complete, execute, conclude, discharge (a debt):&#8212;accomplish, make an end, expire, fill up, finish, go over, pay, perform.";
Lex["5056"] = "telos {tel'-os}|AV - end 35, custom 3, uttermost 1, finally 1, ending 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;by (one's) continual + 1519 1; 42|from a primary tello (to set out for a definite point or goal)|TDNT - 8:49,1161|noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> endINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> termination, the limit at which a thing ceases to be (always of the end of some act or state, but not of the end of a period of time)INDENT3-- <b>b)</b> the endINDENT7--<b>1)</b> the last in any succession or series<BR>INDENT7--<b>2)</b> eternalINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> that by which a thing is finished, its close, issueINDENT3-- <b>d)</b> the end to which all things relate, the aim, purposeINDENT0--<b>2)</b> toll, custom (i.e. indirect tax on goods)<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τέλος t&#xE9;los, tel&#39;-os; from a primary &#x3C4;&#x1F73;&#x3BB;&#x3BB;&#x3C9; t&#xE9;ll&#x14D; (to set out for a definite point or goal); properly, the point aimed at as a limit, i.e. (by implication) the conclusion of an act or state (termination (literally, figuratively or indefinitely), result (immediate, ultimate or prophetic), purpose); specially, an impost or levy (as paid):&#8212;<sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><b>X</b></span></a></sup>continual, custom, end(-ing), finally, uttermost. Compare Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5411&page=1\">G5411</a>.";
Lex["5057"] = "telones {tel-o'-nace}|AV - publican 22; 22|from 5056 and 5608|TDNT - 8:88,1166|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a renter or farmer of taxesINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> among the Romans, usually a man of equestrian rankINDENT0--<b>2)</b> a tax gatherer, collector of taxes or tolls, one employed by a publican or farmer general in the collection of taxes. The tax collectors were as a class, detested not only by the Jews, but by other nations also, both on account of their employment and of the harshness, greed, and deception, with which they did their job.<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τελώνης tel&#x1E53;n&#x113;s, tel-o&#39;-nace; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5056&page=1\">G5056</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5608&page=1\">G5608</a>; a tax-farmer, i.e. collector of public revenue:&#8212;publican.";
