Lex["5082"] = "telikoutos {tay-lik-oo'-tos} feminine telikaute {tay-lik-ow'-tay}|AV - so great 3, so mighty 1; 4|from a compound of 3588 with 2245 and 3778||pron|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> of ageINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of such an ageINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> of so great an age, so oldINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> so youngINDENT0--<b>2)</b> of so great a size, in bulkINDENT0--<b>3)</b> such and so great<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τηλικοῦτος t&#x113;liko&#xFB;tos, tay-lik-oo&#39;-tos; from a compound of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3588&page=1\">G3588</a> with Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2245&page=1\">G2245</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3778&page=1\">G3778</a>; such as this, i.e. (in (figurative) magnitude) so vast:&#8212;so great, so mighty.";
Lex["5083"] = "tereo {tay-reh'-o}|AV - keep 57, reserve 8, observe 4, watch 2, preserve 2, keeper 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;hold fast 1; 75|from teros (a watch, perhaps akin to 2334)|TDNT - 8:140,1174|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to attend to carefully, take care ofINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to guardINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> metaph. to keep, one in the state in which he isINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> to observeINDENT3-- <b>d)</b> to reserve: to undergo something<BR> <!--For Synonyms see entry 5874<br />--><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τηρέω t&#x113;r&#xE9;&#x14D;, tay-reh&#39;-o; from &#x3C4;&#x3B5;&#x3C1;&#x1F79;&#x3C2; ter&#xF3;s (a watch; perhaps akin to Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2334&page=1\">G2334</a>); to guard (from loss or injury, properly, by keeping the eye upon; and thus differing from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5442&page=1\">G5442</a>, which is properly to prevent escaping; and from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2892&page=1\">G2892</a>, which implies a fortress or full military lines of apparatus), i.e. to note (a prophecy; figuratively, to fulfil a command); by implication, to detain (in custody; figuratively, to maintain); by extension, to withhold (for personal ends; figuratively, to keep unmarried); by extension, to withhold (for personal ends; figuratively, to keep unmarried):&#8212;hold fast, keep(- er), (pre-, re-)serve, watch.";
