Lex["5177"] = "tugchano {toong-khan'-o}|AV - obtain 5, be 1, chance 1, little 1, enjoy 1, may be 1, not tr 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;misc 2; 13|probably for an obsolete tucho (for which the middle voice of another alternate teucho [to make ready or bring to pass] is used in certain tenses, akin to the base of 5088 through the idea of effecting|TDNT - 8:238,1191|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to hit the markINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of one discharging a javelin or arrowINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to reach, attain, obtain, get, become master ofINDENT0--<b>3)</b> to happen, chance, fall outINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to specify, to take a case, as for exampleINDENT0--<b>4)</b> to meet oneINDENT0--<b>5)</b> of he who meets one or presents himself unsought, any chance, ordinary, common personINDENT0--<b>6)</b> to chance to be<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τυγχάνω tynch&#xE1;n&#x14D;, toong-khan&#39;-o; probably for an obsolete &#x3C4;&#x1F7B;&#x3C7;&#x3C9; t&#xFD;ch&#x14D; (for which the middle voice of another alternate &#x3C4;&#x3B5;&#x1F7B;&#x3C7;&#x3C9; te&#xFA;ch&#x14D; (to make ready or bring to pass) is used in certain tenses; akin to the base of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5088&page=1\">G5088</a> through the idea of effecting; properly, to affect; or (specially), to hit or light upon (as a mark to be reached), i.e. (transitively) to attain or secure an object or end, or (intransitively) to happen (as if meeting with); but in the latter application only impersonal (with Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1487&page=1\">G1487</a>), i.e. perchance; or (present participle) as adjective, usual (as if commonly met with, with Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3756&page=1\">G3756</a>, extraordinary), neuter (as adverb) perhaps; or (with another verb) as adverb, by accident (as it were):&#8212;be, chance, enjoy, little, obtain, <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><b>X</b></a></sup>refresh&#8230;self, <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><b>X</b></span></a></sup>special. Compare Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5180&page=1\">G5180</a>.";
Lex["5178"] = "tumpanizo {toom-pan-id'-zo}|AV - torture 1; 1|from a derivative of 5180 (meaning a drum, \"tympanum\")||verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to beat the drum or timbrelINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to torture with the tympanum, an instrument of punishment<BR><BR> The tympanum seems to have been a wheel shaped instrument of torture, over which criminals were stretched as though they were skins and then horribly beaten with clubs or thongs (cf our \"break upon the wheel\")<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τυμπανίζω tympan&#xED;z&#x14D;, toom-pan-id&#39;-zo; from a derivative of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5180&page=1\">G5180</a> (meaning a drum, \"tympanum\"); to stretch on an instrument of torture resembling a drum, and thus beat to death:&#8212;torture.";
Lex["5179"] = "tupos {too'-pos}|AV - ensample 5, print 2, figure 2, example 2, pattern 2, fashion 1,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;manner 1, form 1; 16|from 5180|TDNT - 8:246,1193|noun masculine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> the mark of a stroke or blow, printINDENT0--<b>2)</b> a figure formed by a blow or impressionINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> of a figure or imageINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> of the image of the godsINDENT0--<b>3)</b> formINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> the teaching which embodies the sum and substance of religion and represents it to the mind, manner of writing, the contents and form of a letterINDENT0--<b>4)</b> an exampleINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> in the technical sense, the pattern in conformity to which a thing must be madeINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> in an ethical sense, a dissuasive example, a pattern of warningINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of ruinous events which serve as admonitions or warnings to othersINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> an example to be imitatedINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of men worthy of imitationINDENT3-- <b>d)</b> in a doctrinal senseINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of a type i.e. a person or thing prefiguring a future (Messianic) person or thing<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>τύπος t&#xFD;pos, too&#39;-pos; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5180&page=1\">G5180</a>; a die (as struck), i.e. (by implication) a stamp or scar; by analogy, a shape, i.e. a statue, (figuratively) style or resemblance; specially, a sampler ( \"type\"), i.e. a model (for imitation) or instance (for warning):&#8212;en-(ex-)ample, fashion, figure, form, manner, pattern, print.";
Lex["5180"] = "tupto {toop'-to}|AV - smite 9, beat 3, strike 1, wound 1; 14|a primary verb (in a strengthened form)|TDNT - 8:260,1195|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to strike, beat, smiteINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> with a staff, a whip, the fist, the handINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> of mourners, to smite their breastINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to smite one on whom he inflicts punitive evilINDENT0--<b>3)</b> to smiteINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> metaph. i.e. to wound, disquiet one's conscience<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> τύπτω t&#xFD;pt&#x14D;, toop&#39;-to; a primary verb (in a strengthened form); to \"thump\", i.e. cudgel or pummel (properly, with a stick or bastinado), but in any case by repeated blows; thus differing from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3817&page=1\">G3817</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3960&page=1\">G3960</a>, which denote a (usually single) blow with the hand or any instrument, or Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4141&page=1\">G4141</a> with the fist (or a hammer), or Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=4474&page=1\">G4474</a> with the palm; as well as from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5177&page=1\">G5177</a>, an accidental collision); by implication, to punish; figuratively, to offend (the conscience):&#8212;beat, smite, strike, wound.";
