Lex["5342"] = "phero {fer'-o}|AV - bring 34, bear 8, bring forth 5, come 3, reach 2, endure 2,<BR> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;carry 1, misc 9; 64|a primary verb (for which other and apparently not cognate ones are used in certain tenses only, namely, oio {oy'-o}; and enegko {en-eng'-ko)|TDNT - 9:56,1252|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to carryINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to carry some burdenINDENT7--<b>1)</b> to bear with one's selfINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to move by bearing; move or, to be conveyed or borne, with the suggestion of force or speedINDENT7--<b>1)</b> of persons borne in a ship over the seaINDENT7--<b>2)</b> of a gust of wind, to rushINDENT7--<b>3)</b> of the mind, to be moved inwardly, prompted<BR>INDENT3-- <b>c)</b> to bear up i.e. uphold (keep from falling)INDENT7--<b>1)</b> of Christ, the preserver of the universeINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to bear, i.e. endure, to endure the rigour of a thing, to bear patiently one's conduct, or spare one (abstain from punishing or destroying)INDENT0--<b>3)</b> to bring, bring to, bring forwardINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to move to, applyINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to bring in by announcing, to announceINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> to bear i.e. bring forth, produce; to bring forward in a speechINDENT3-- <b>d)</b> to lead, conduct<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> φέρω ph&#xE9;r&#x14D;, fer&#39;-o; a primary verb (for which other, and apparently not cognate ones are used in certain tenses only; namely, &#x3BF;&#x1F34;&#x3C9; o&#xED;&#x14D; oy&#39;-o; and &#x1F10;&#x3BD;&#x1F73;&#x3B3;&#x3BA;&#x3C9; en&#xE9;nk&#x14D; en-eng&#39;-ko; to \"bear\" or carry (in a very wide application, literally and figuratively, as follows):&#8212;be, bear, bring (forth), carry, come, <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><b>X</b></span></a></sup>let her drive, be driven, endure, go on, lay, lead, move, reach, rushing, uphold.";
