Lex["5368"] = "phileo {fil-eh'-o}|AV - love 22, kiss 3; 25|from 5384|TDNT - 9:114,1262|verb|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> to loveINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to approve ofINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> to likeINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> sanctionINDENT3-- <b>d)</b> to treat affectionately or kindly, to welcome, befriendINDENT0--<b>2)</b> to show signs of loveINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> to kissINDENT0--<b>3)</b> to be fond of doingINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> be wont, use to do<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> φιλέω phil&#xE9;&#x14D;, fil-eh&#39;-o; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5384&page=1\">G5384</a>; to be a friend to (fond of (an individual or an object)), i.e. have affection for (denoting personal attachment, as a matter of sentiment or feeling; while Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=25&page=1\">G25</a> is wider, embracing especially the judgment and the deliberate assent of the will as a matter of principle, duty and propriety: the two thus stand related very much as Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2309&page=1\">G2309</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1014&page=1\">G1014</a>, or as Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=2372&page=1\">G2372</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=3563&page=1\">G3563</a> respectively; the former being chiefly of the heart and the latter of the head); specially, to kiss (as a mark of tenderness):&#8212;kiss, love.";
