Lex["5384"] = "philos {fee'-los}|AV - friend 29; 29|a primitive word|TDNT - 9:146,1262|adjective|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> friend, to be friendly to one, wish him wellINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> a friendINDENT3-- <b>b)</b> an associateINDENT3-- <b>c)</b> he who associates familiarly with one, a companionINDENT3-- <b>d)</b> one of the bridegroom's friends who on his behalf asked the hand of the bride and rendered him various services in closing the marriage and celebrating the nuptials<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> <sup><a href=\"#strongs-legend\"><span style=\"font-size:150%\"><b>&dagger;</b></span></a></sup>φίλος ph&#xED;los, fee&#39;-los; properly, dear, i.e. a friend; actively, fond, i.e. friendly (still as a noun, an associate, neighbor, etc.):&#8212;friend.";
Lex["5385"] = "philosophia {fil-os-of-ee'-ah}|AV - philosophy 1; 1|from 5386|TDNT - 9:172,1269|noun feminine|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> love of wisdomINDENT3-- <b>a)</b> used either of zeal for or skill in any art or science, any branch of knowledge. Used once in the NT of the theology, or rather theosophy, of certain Jewish Christian ascetics, which busied itself with refined and speculative enquiries into the nature and classes of angels, into the ritual of the Mosaic law and the regulations of Jewish tradition respecting practical life<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> φιλοσοφία philosoph&#xED;a, fil-os-of-ee&#39;-ah; from Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5386&page=1\">G5386</a>; \"philosophy\", i.e. (specially), Jewish sophistry:&#8212;philosophy.";
