Lex["5498"] = "cheirographon {khi-rog'-raf-on}|AV - handwriting 1; 1|from a compound of 5495 and 1125|TDNT - 9:435,1309|noun neuter|INDENT0--<b>1)</b> a handwriting, what one has written by his own handINDENT0--<b>2)</b> a note of hand or writing in which one acknowledges that money has either been deposited with him or lent to him by another, to be returned at the appointed time<br /><BR /><hr />INDENT0--<b>Strong\'s Definition</b><br> χειρόγραφον cheir&#xF3;graphon, khi-rog&#39;-raf-on; neuter of a compound of Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=5495&page=1\">G5495</a> and Strong\'s <a href=\"strongs_greek.html?strongs=1125&page=1\">G1125</a>; something hand-written ( \"chirograph\"), i.e. a manuscript (specially, a legal document or bond (figuratively)):&#8212;handwriting.";
